Alembic migrations of the backend (async dbapi; env.py builds the URL from DATABASE_*).

Revisions: versions/0001_initial.py (down_revision None) holds every table, index and
constraint of the development schema, the row-level security policies of the agent role
and its column grant on documents; versions/0002_project_collaborators.py (project
collaborators) is the first incremental revision: it reshapes the member roles, adds
project_invites and keeps a legacy trigger for the rolling deploy (docs/projects/data-model.md).

On a schema change:

1. Edit the models (src/db/models.py) and write the revision by hand (do not
   autogenerate it); keep sql-schema.json in step.
2. `make db-upgrade` applies it (the api container also runs `specflow migrate` on start).
3. Check it: from backend/ `uv run --env-file ../.env.local alembic check` (the models
   match the revisions) and `uv run --env-file ../.env.local alembic current` (prints
   `0002_project_collaborators (head)`).

A database stamped with a revision that no longer exists (for example `0005` from the
old chain) makes `alembic upgrade` fail with "Can't locate revision"; recreate it with `make down-volumes` and `make up`. downgrade() of 0001 drops every table it created;
downgrade() of 0002 deletes collaborator rows and invites (data loss).

migrations/sql/ holds the SQL text the revisions read with their own read_migration_sql
(the revisions never import src/).
